  "id": "t13-overrides-model-provider-effort-atomic-swap-post-body",
  "description": "T13 bilateral CLI observation (expected match), item 16 of the versioned inventory (contract decision 13/L13): spawn_session's model and effort overrides both land in the SAME single upstream POST body the child's first request sends — model as the top-level 'model' field, effort as 'reasoning_effort' (contract L9's own wire mapping for the chat-completions transport, confirmed byte-measured earlier this ticket). Scoped to same-provider (model+effort only, staying on 'ollama' so the single stub server can observe the child's own request directly) — a full cross-provider swap (decision 13's 'provider' override, which atomically swaps provider+client+model together) would need a second, differently-shaped upstream endpoint and is deferred to a live-smoke-style harness rather than this stub, per the same reasoning T10's own live-smoke scenarios were split out for. KNOWN LIMIT (declared, not a gap to fix): events.requests is excluded from bilateral comparisons — the child's request arrival position relative to the parent's own is the same scheduler-dependent, stable-but-different-per-side class documented in section O and reproduced in items 6-9. The override fields' presence and values are instead verified via side-scoped expectations at each side's own stable index.",
